<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <title>AArch64 Autopilot — Evidence Report</title>
  <style>
    :root { --bg:#050b14; --panel:#0b1728; --line:#21334a; --text:#f8fafc; --muted:#9fb0c5; --mint:#3ddc97; --cyan:#38bdf8; --amber:#fbbf24; }
    * { box-sizing:border-box; }
    body { margin:0; color:var(--text); background:radial-gradient(circle at 84% 0,#12304d 0,transparent 30%),var(--bg); font:16px/1.55 ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif; }
    main { width:min(1180px,calc(100% - 40px)); margin:auto; padding:48px 0 80px; }
    .skip { position:absolute; left:16px; top:-80px; z-index:10; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px; color:#00140c; background:var(--mint); font-weight:800; }
    .skip:focus { top:16px; }
    nav { position:sticky; top:12px; z-index:5; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px; width:max-content; max-width:100%; padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:999px; background:rgba(5,11,20,.92); backdrop-filter:blur(12px); }
    nav a { color:#dbeafe; text-decoration:none; padding:7px 11px; border-radius:999px; font-size:.82rem; font-weight:700; }
    nav a:hover,nav a:focus-visible { color:#00140c; background:var(--mint); outline:none; }
    header[id],section[id] { scroll-margin-top:88px; }
    header { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.35fr .65fr; gap:28px; align-items:end; padding:32px 0 38px; }
    .eyebrow { color:var(--mint); letter-spacing:.16em; text-transform:uppercase; font-size:.78rem; font-weight:800; }
    h1 { font-size:clamp(2.6rem,6vw,5.8rem); line-height:.94; letter-spacing:-.055em; margin:.25em 0; max-width:900px; }
    h2 { font-size:1.55rem; letter-spacing:-.02em; margin:0 0 18px; }
    p { color:var(--muted); }
    .status { border:1px solid var(--line); background:rgba(11,23,40,.84); padding:22px; border-radius:18px; }
    .status strong { color:{% if evidence_status == 'measured' %}var(--mint){% else %}var(--amber){% endif %}; display:block; font-size:1.2rem; }
    .badges { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:10px; margin-top:22px; }
    .badge { padding:8px 11px; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:999px; color:#dbeafe; background:#07111f; font-size:.82rem; }
    .grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(12,1fr); gap:18px; margin:18px 0; }
    .card { grid-column:span 4; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:18px; padding:22px; background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgba(16,34,56,.92),rgba(8,19,34,.95)); min-height:155px; }
    .card.wide { grid-column:span 6; }
    .metric { font-size:2rem; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:-.035em; color:var(--mint); }
    .metric small { font-size:.8rem; color:var(--muted); display:block; letter-spacing:0; font-weight:500; }
    table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; background:var(--panel); border-radius:16px; overflow:hidden; }
    th,td { text-align:left; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); padding:13px 15px; }
    th { color:#cbd5e1; font-size:.76rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em; }
    td { color:var(--muted); }
    .figure { width:100%; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:18px; display:block; }
    code { color:#bae6fd; }
    footer { border-top:1px solid var(--line); margin-top:42px; padding-top:24px; color:var(--muted); font-size:.88rem; }
    @media(max-width:800px){header{grid-template-columns:1fr}header[id],section[id]{scroll-margin-top:176px}.card,.card.wide{grid-column:span 12}}
  </style>
</head>
<body><a class="skip" href="#overview">Skip to report</a><main>
  <nav aria-label="Report sections">
    <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
    <a href="#target">Target</a>
    <a href="#candidates">Candidates</a>
    <a href="#probes">Probes</a>
    <a href="#cascade">A4 cascade</a>
    <a href="#figures">Figures</a>
    <a href="#evidence">Evidence</a>
    <a href="#limitations">Limitations</a>
  </nav>
  <header id="overview">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">CPU-only Arm AI optimization</div>
      <h1>AArch64<br>Autopilot</h1>
      <p>A bounded tuner, quality gate, OpenAI-compatible endpoint, and claim-level evidence pipeline for agentic inference on Arm64 CPUs.</p>
      <div class="badges"><span class="badge">GPU: NONE</span><span class="badge">QUALITY-GATED</span><span class="badge">RAW EVIDENCE</span><span class="badge">OPEN SOURCE</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="status">
      <strong>{% if evidence_status == 'measured' %}MEASURED EVIDENCE{% else %}ARM64 MEASUREMENT PENDING{% endif %}</strong>
      <p>{% if evidence_status == 'measured' %}{{ measurement_count }} measured request rows passed provenance checks.{% else %}No performance number is published until the fair generic/KleidiAI run finishes on Arm64 Linux. {{ fixture_count }} fixture rows remain excluded.{% endif %}</p>
      <p>Cases <code>{{ cases_sha256[:12] }}…</code><br>Split v{{ split_schema_version }} <code>{{ split_sha256[:12] }}…</code></p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="grid">
    {% if claims %}
      {% for claim in claims %}
      <article class="card"><div class="metric">{{ '%.2f'|format(claim.value) }}{{ claim.unit }}<small>{% if claim.claim_id == primary_claim_id %}PRIMARY — {% else %}SECONDARY — {% endif %}{{ claim.metric }}</small></div><p>{% if claim.confidence_interval[0] > 0 %}Interval excludes zero on the positive side.{% elif claim.confidence_interval[1] < 0 %}Interval excludes zero on the negative side.{% else %}Interval crosses zero.{% endif %} {% if claim.claim_id == primary_claim_id %}{% if claim.demonstrated %}The preregistered final gate passes.{% else %}The final gate does not pass.{% endif %}{% else %}Disclosed transparently; never unlocks final publication.{% endif %}</p></article>
      {% endfor %}
    {% else %}
      <article class="card"><div class="metric">0<small>fabricated benchmark claims</small></div><p>The report fails closed when target evidence is absent.</p></article>
    {% endif %}
    <article class="card"><div class="metric">100%<small>required safety floor</small></div><p>The submitted strong-only proxy validates schema, read-only tool policy, safety, and consistency; invalid output fails closed with HTTP 502.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="metric">40 / 20<small>calibration / v2 final-holdout cases</small></div><p>{% if cascade_status is defined and cascade_status %}A4 status: <code>{{ cascade_status.get("status", "unknown") }}</code>. Shipping: <code>{{ cascade_status.get("shipping_profile", cascade_status.get("shipping_fallback", "not selected")) }}</code>.{% else %}A4 has not been calibrated; the measured strong-only profile remains the fallback.{% endif %}</p></article>
  </section>

  <section id="target"><h2>Target provenance</h2>
    {% if system is defined and system %}
    <table><tbody>
      <tr><th>Architecture</th><td><code>{{ system.get("architecture", "not exposed") }}</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th>CPU model</th><td><code>{{ system.get("cpu_model", "not exposed") }}</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th>Distribution</th><td>{{ (system.get("distribution") or {}).get("pretty_name", "not exposed") }}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Kernel</th><td><code>{{ system.get("kernel", "not exposed") }}</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th>Topology</th><td>{{ system.get("physical_cores", "not exposed") }} physical / {{ system.get("logical_cores", "not exposed") }} logical cores; {{ system.get("sockets", "not exposed") }} socket(s); {{ system.get("numa_nodes", "not exposed") }} NUMA node(s)</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Memory</th><td>{{ system.get("memory_bytes", "not exposed") }} bytes</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Compiler</th><td><code>{{ system.get("tool_versions", {}).get("compiler", "not exposed") }}</code></td></tr>
      {% for cache in system.get("cache_layout", []) %}<tr><th>{{ cache.get("name", "cache")|upper }}</th><td>{{ cache.get("total_size_bytes", "not exposed") }} bytes across {{ cache.get("instances", "not exposed") }} instance(s), from {{ cache.get("source", "unknown source") }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    </tbody></table>
    {% if system.get("target_provenance_status") == "complete" %}<p>The validated SystemInfo v2 schema marks target provenance complete: CPU model, distribution, physical cores, memory, compiler, socket, NUMA, L1d/L1i/L2/L3 caches, instruction-feature evidence, per-core topology, and affinity candidates were exposed.</p>{% else %}<p><strong>Validated SystemInfo v2 status: limited.</strong></p><ul>{% for item in system.get("provenance_limitations", []) %}<li><code>{{ item.get("code", "unknown") }}</code> (<code>{{ item.get("field", "unknown") }}</code>): {{ item.get("reason", "no reason recorded") }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
    {% else %}<p>No target manifest is available; performance evidence remains pending.</p>{% endif %}
  </section>

  <section id="candidates"><h2>Measured candidates</h2>
    <table><thead><tr><th>Candidate</th><th>Stage</th><th>Backend</th><th>n</th><th>p50 ms</th><th>p95 ms</th><th>Quality</th><th>Safety</th><th>Peak RSS</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{% if summaries %}{% for row in summaries %}<tr><td>{{ row.candidate_id }}</td><td>{{ row.stage }}</td><td>{{ row.backend }}</td><td>{{ row.sample_count }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.p50_latency_ms) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.p95_latency_ms) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.quality_score) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.safety_score) }}</td><td>{{ '%.1f'|format(row.peak_rss_mb) }} MB</td></tr>{% endfor %}{% else %}<tr><td colspan="9">Awaiting same-machine Arm64 Linux A1/A2 measurements.</td></tr>{% endif %}</tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="probes" style="margin-top:28px"><h2>Supporting protocol probes</h2>
    {% if formal_repetitions_per_case is defined and formal_repetitions_per_case %}<p>The formal fair A1/A2 holdout used <strong>{{ formal_repetitions_per_case }} quality repetition(s) per case</strong>. {% if formal_repetitions_per_case == 1 %}This is the disclosed reduced-run design: one quality repetition on each of 20 frozen holdout cases plus the independent repeated probes below.{% else %}The probes remain separate supporting evidence.{% endif %}</p>{% if formal_sample_disclosure is defined and formal_sample_disclosure %}<p><strong>Formal sample disclosure:</strong> {{ formal_sample_disclosure.paired_case_count }} paired cases; {{ formal_sample_disclosure.measured_rows }} / {{ formal_sample_disclosure.expected_rows }} expected A1/A2 rows; {{ formal_sample_disclosure.failed_or_missing_rows }} failed or missing rows. An incomplete pair fails the claim/report gate.</p>{% endif %}{% else %}<p>Formal quality repetition count is pending.</p>{% endif %}
    {% if performance_probes is defined and performance_probes %}
    <p><strong>Scope:</strong> supporting ranking/concurrency evidence, not a held-out headline claim. {{ performance_probes.repetitions }} measured repetitions/rounds; topology-derived threads {{ performance_probes.micro_threads|join(", ") }}; fixed calibration case <code>{{ performance_probes.case_id }}</code>. The artifact carries a complete raw-file integrity manifest refreshed after public redaction.</p><p><strong>Semantic replay:</strong> {{ performance_probes.semantic_replay_verified }}; fingerprint <code>{{ performance_probes.semantic_sha256 }}</code>. {{ performance_probes.micro_cells }} micro cells / {{ performance_probes.micro_underlying_measurements }} underlying pp/tg measurements; {{ performance_probes.service_rounds }} service rounds / {{ performance_probes.service_requests }} measured requests. Protocol failures: {{ performance_probes.failed_micro_cells }} micro cells, {{ performance_probes.failed_service_rounds }} service rounds; any protocol failure prevents a complete artifact. Measured service responses include <strong>{{ performance_probes.measured_service_safety_pass_count }} safety passes and {{ performance_probes.measured_service_safety_failure_count }} recorded safety failures</strong>. Calibration-case safety/quality outcomes are retained without filtering and support no held-out safety or quality claim.</p>
    {% if probe_provenance is defined and probe_provenance %}<h3>Build and model provenance</h3><p><code>{{ probe_provenance.source_url }}</code> at commit <code>{{ probe_provenance.source_commit }}</code>.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Build</th><th>CPU-only</th><th>KleidiAI configured</th><th>Runtime proof</th><th>llama-bench SHA-256</th><th>llama-server SHA-256</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in probe_provenance.build_variants %}<tr><td>{{ row.backend }}</td><td>{{ row.cpu_only_configured }}</td><td>{{ row.kleidiai_configured }}</td><td>{{ row.runtime_marker_verified }}</td><td><code>{{ row.llama_bench_sha256 }}</code></td><td><code>{{ row.llama_server_sha256 }}</code></td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Quant</th><th>Exact bytes</th><th>SHA-256</th><th>Tensor inventory SHA-256</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in probe_provenance.models %}<tr><td><code>{{ row.filename }}</code></td><td>{{ row.quantization }}</td><td>{{ row.bytes }}</td><td><code>{{ row.sha256 }}</code></td><td><code>{{ row.tensor_inventory_sha256 }}</code></td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>{% endif %}
    <h3>Microbenchmark matrix</h3>
    <table><thead><tr><th>Backend</th><th>Quant</th><th>Threads</th><th>Test</th><th>n</th><th>tokens/s mean</th><th>tokens/s sd</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in performance_probes.micro %}<tr><td>{{ row.backend }}</td><td>{{ row.quantization }}</td><td>{{ row.threads }}</td><td>{{ row.test }}</td><td>{{ row.repetitions }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.tokens_per_second) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.tokens_per_second_stddev) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
    <h3>Fresh-start p1/p2 service probes</h3>
    <table><thead><tr><th>Backend</th><th>p</th><th>Startup ms</th><th>Rounds / requests</th><th>Safety pass / fail</th><th>Quality mean / min</th><th>Prompt / completion tokens</th><th>req/s mean ± sd</th><th>generated tok/s mean ± sd</th><th>per-request gen tok/s mean ± sd</th><th>TTFT p50 / p95 ms</th><th>E2E p50 / p95 ms</th><th>Idle / peak RSS MiB</th><th>Context total / slot</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in performance_probes.service %}<tr><td>{{ row.backend }}</td><td>{{ row.parallel }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.startup_ms) }}</td><td>{{ row.rounds }} / {{ row.requests }}</td><td>{{ row.safety_pass_count }} / {{ row.safety_failure_count }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.quality_score_mean) }} / {{ '%.2f'|format(row.quality_score_min) }}</td><td>{{ row.prompt_tokens_total }} / {{ row.completion_tokens_total }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(row.requests_per_second_mean) }} ± {{ '%.3f'|format(row.requests_per_second_stddev) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.generated_tokens_per_second_mean) }} ± {{ '%.2f'|format(row.generated_tokens_per_second_stddev) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.request_generation_tok_s_mean) }} ± {{ '%.2f'|format(row.request_generation_tok_s_stddev) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.ttft_p50_ms) }} / {{ '%.2f'|format(row.ttft_p95_ms) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(row.e2e_p50_ms) }} / {{ '%.2f'|format(row.e2e_p95_ms) }}</td><td>{{ '%.1f'|format(row.idle_rss_mb) }} / {{ '%.1f'|format(row.peak_rss_mb) }}</td><td>{{ row.context_total }} / {{ row.context_per_slot }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
    <p>For p2, total context is doubled so each in-flight request retains the same 2048-token capacity as p1. Round wall time derives completed requests/s and aggregate generated tokens/s; completion usage plus monotonic first/end timestamps replay per-request generation rate. Missing usage, first token, schema-valid output, complete <code>stop</code> finish, raw hash, or matrix cell fails closed. A schema-valid safety failure is recorded, not dropped or retried, so performance statistics are not conditioned on a favorable safety result.</p><p><strong>Exact reproduction commands:</strong></p><ul>{% for command in performance_probes.reproduction_commands %}<li><code>{{ command }}</code></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {% else %}<p>Supporting micro/startup/token/p1/p2 evidence is pending and contributes no claim.</p>{% endif %}
  </section>

  <section id="cascade" style="margin-top:28px"><h2>A4 quality-gated cascade</h2>
    {% if cascade_status is defined and cascade_status %}<p><strong>{{ cascade_status.get("status", "unknown") }}</strong> — {{ cascade_status.get("reason", "No A4 reason was recorded.") }}</p>{% else %}<p>A4 calibration has not run.</p>{% endif %}
    {% if cascade_quality is defined and cascade_quality and cascade_quality.get("held_out") %}<div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="metric">{{ '%.2f'|format(cascade_quality["held_out"]["route_shares"]["weak"]) }}%<small>weak final route</small></div></article><article class="card"><div class="metric">{{ '%.2f'|format(cascade_quality["held_out"]["route_shares"]["strong"]) }}%<small>direct strong route</small></div></article><article class="card"><div class="metric">{{ '%.2f'|format(cascade_quality["held_out"]["route_shares"]["weak_then_strong"]) }}%<small>automatic weak→strong escalation</small></div></article></div><p>Escalation rate: {{ '%.2f'|format(cascade_quality["held_out"]["escalation_rate"]) }}% of weak attempts. Quality replay gate: {% if cascade_quality["held_out"]["gate"]["passed"] %}pass{% else %}rejected; strong-only fallback retained{% endif %}. {{ cascade_quality["held_out"].get("evaluation_design", "Component replay is quality/routing evidence only") }}. It is ineligible for live-cascade latency, throughput, or combined-memory claims. Live A4 combined RSS is <strong>not measured and not eligible</strong>.</p>{% endif %}
  </section>

  <section id="figures" class="grid" style="margin-top:28px"><article class="card wide"><img class="figure" src="figures/ablation.png" alt="Ablation stages"></article><article class="card wide"><img class="figure" src="figures/pareto.png" alt="Quality latency Pareto candidates"></article></section>
  <section id="evidence"><h2>Evidence contract</h2><p>The primary Arm claim compares the same Q4_0 model checksum, prompts, sampling, runtime settings, CPU affinity, and machine. The exact pinned strong-model inventory contains 197 Q4_0 tensors and one disclosed Q6_K <code>output.weight</code>; that fallback is allowed only when SHA-256, size, and the full GGUF header inventory match. The primary KleidiAI Q4 marker is required and any additional or different fallback is rejected. The intended change is only the generic versus KleidiAI backend. Every report claim retains its raw run IDs and explicit formula; fixture output can never support a claim.</p><p>Split v1's test cases were executed during failed run6 and used for error analysis, so they are retired from final evaluation. Split v2 keeps its frozen 20-case membership and primary definition; this cycle is an unchanged-split replication/revalidation, not unseen or newly held-out evidence. <code>demo/split-freeze-v2.json</code> preserves the audit trail.</p><p>Mean TTFT reduction is the prospectively registered primary outcome. P95 end-to-end latency reduction and median per-request throughput increase are transparent secondary outcomes. All three use the same {{ formal_sample_disclosure.paired_case_count if formal_sample_disclosure is defined and formal_sample_disclosure else 20 }} paired cases and {{ formal_sample_disclosure.measured_rows if formal_sample_disclosure is defined and formal_sample_disclosure else "the recorded" }} formal A1/A2 source rows. Only a positive primary interval with a lower bound above zero unlocks final publication.</p><p>The deployed profile remains strong-only until a separately measured live A4 performance run exists. A4 quality admission never substitutes component replay timings for live multi-runtime evidence.</p><p>The repository carries sanitized formal rows and <code>claims.json</code>; the attested release bundle carries the full redacted raw capture and integrity receipts.</p></section>
  <section id="limitations"><h2>Limitations</h2><ul>{% for limitation in limitations %}<li>{{ limitation }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></section>
  <footer>Generated {{ generated_at }} from local artifacts. This file loads no external network resources.</footer>
</main></body></html>
